--[[
	ApplyPropMeshes (dev tool, Edit mode only) - Blender props -> ServerStorage.MapProps.<propId> -> SyncMapProps.run.
	docs/model_upgrade_brief.txt section 5; contract: Blender/Props/README.txt section 7 (Agent A).
	Source of truth: tools/ApplyPropMeshes.luau. Data: ServerStorage.DevTools.PropMeshData = a paste of
	Blender_Exports/Props/PropMeshData.luau (generated by Agent A; paste it again whenever it is regenerated).

	After the owner's import of Blender_Exports/Props/<propId>.fbx (File > Import 3D, preset "Studio Default":
	Scale Unit = Studs, Merge Meshes OFF; Blender_Exports/Props/PROPS_IMPORT.md), the imported Models at the top of
	the Workspace or in Workspace.ImportedProps / ServerStorage.ImportedProps:
		print(require(game.ServerStorage.DevTools.ApplyPropMeshes:Clone()).run())
		print(require(game.ServerStorage.DevTools.ApplyPropMeshes:Clone()).run({ only = { "well" } }))  -- some props
		print(require(game.ServerStorage.DevTools.ApplyPropMeshes:Clone()).run({ dryRun = true }))      -- report only
	For every prop of PropMeshData.Props whose import is found it first CHECKS the import against the data and SKIPS
	the prop (today's template and models stay untouched, the report says why) when:
	  - a mesh of the data is missing (render or collider mesh), or the import holds a mesh the data does not know
	    (Merge Meshes was ON?), or two meshes share a name (only run({ allowMissing = true }) accepts missing / extra
	    meshes);
	  - a mesh is rotated (more than 2 degrees off the import's identity: World Forward / Up changed?);
	  - a mesh's size is not its data size times ONE factor on all axes (distorted), or the meshes disagree on that
	    factor; one common factor (a wrong import Scale Unit: 28x, 100x, 0.036x ...) is fine: every mesh is resized;
	  - the meshes' positions relative to each other are not the data's (a turned / mirrored / moved import);
	  - a preview of the prop is installed (endPreview first).
	Then it builds the template ServerStorage.MapProps.<propId>:
	  - the meshes are looked up by their data name (<propId>_<Part>) BEFORE they are renamed <Part>;
	  - Size = the data Size; CFrame = pivot * CFrame.new(Center) (no rotation), PivotOffset = CFrame.new(Pivot - Center);
	  - Anchored, CanCollide false, CanTouch false, CanQuery false, CollisionFidelity Box (collider meshes Hull: set on a
	    short visit of the new template to a stage in the Workspace far from the map, the only place where Studio
	    applies it), CastShadow from the data;
	  - role from the data (Role, or the _Glow / _Water / _Glass / _Stream / _Foam suffix): Glow = Neon + Color;
	    Water = Glass + Transparency + the water_ripple Texture ("Ripples") on the top face; Stream (falling water) =
	    Glass + Transparency 0.45 + "Ripples" on the four side faces; Foam = SmoothPlastic + Transparency 0.2; Glass =
	    Transparency; none of them has a SurfaceAppearance. Otherwise Material from the data and a SurfaceAppearance
	    of the family's shared texture set with SurfaceAppearance.Color = the data tint (imported SAs are replaced);
	  - invisible collider Parts from the data (Block / Cylinder / Wedge / Ball, Roblox orientation in degrees), and
	    collider meshes (data Role "Collider") as invisible Hull colliders of their data Size; render meshes never
	    collide;
	  - an invisible "Root" Part (Bounds) as PrimaryPart, pivot (0, PivotY, 0), the data Attachments under Root,
	    the static lights of Config/PropFX (Lights, on the part "<Part>" / "<Part>_Glow" or on an Attachment) and
	    its particle emitters (Particles, off), the recolour variants of VARIANTS (or the old template's _Variants),
	    DROP_ATTRIBUTES;
	the old template goes to ServerStorage.MapProps._Previous, then SyncMapProps.run updates the test area and the map.
	A new template identical to the current one (a second run) is not installed again ("unchanged"), so _Previous keeps
	the real previous template. After a successful (or unchanged) apply the imported Model moves to
	ServerStorage.ImportedProps (not visible, kept as the source of later runs; an older import of the same name goes
	to ServerStorage.ImportedProps._Replaced).

	"Pieces only" props (PIECES below: the 3 stalls; data Placement "pieces only"): the FBX holds only the Blender
	pieces (awning, display items, sign, gems); the frame is the Studio-built template. The new template = a copy of
	that frame template (the base; saved once in MapProps._Base.<propId> by the first real run, so later runs start
	from the same frame) where:
	  - every mesh with an Anchor is re-based on the real part it was modelled on (README section 7, world CFrames):
	        assumed = stallPivot * CFrame.new(AssumedPosition) * CFrame.fromOrientation(rotation in degrees)
	        MeshPart.CFrame = realPart.CFrame * assumed:Inverse() * (stallPivot * CFrame.new(Center))
	    realPart = the part named Anchor.Part (of size PartSize when there is one) nearest to the assumed position;
	    meshes without an anchor go to stallPivot * CFrame.new(Center);
	  - the replaced parts (PIECES[propId].Remove, = the data Replaces) leave; the ones that collided stay as invisible
	    colliders "Collider_<Name>" (solid stays solid) unless a data collider takes over (DataColliders: the awning);
	  - the data colliders, an invisible "PiecesRoot" part holding the data Attachments (an attachment inside an
	    anchored item moves with it), the PropFX lights / emitters; attribute MapPropPieces.
	Nested props (anvil_forge = the AnvilForge sub-model of each weapon stall, data Placement.OriginInHost) are normal
	templates synced over their nested instances; preview / run check the host offset against OriginInHost.

	Studio preview without an import (Agent A encodes a prop's meshes in PNGs, README "Preview images"):
		print(Apply.preview("well", { "rbxassetid://<id>" }))   -- decode, build, install, sync (TEMPORARY)
		print(Apply.endPreview("well"))                          -- back to the template that was there before
	Preview MeshParts are EditableMesh-backed: they do not survive a save, so endPreview must run before any save.
	preview() keeps the untouched originals in MapProps._PreviewHold.<propId>; endPreview() puts them back exactly
	(same instances) and restores the previous template; a collider mesh (never in the PNG) gets a stand-in box.
	A second preview of the same prop is refused until endPreview (it would lose the real previous template), and run()
	skips a prop while its preview is installed.
	A nested prop and its host (anvil_forge in weapon_stall): end the previews in the reverse order (the host first).
]]
local AssetService = game:GetService("AssetService")
local CollectionService = game:GetService("CollectionService")
local HttpService = game:GetService("HttpService")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local ServerStorage = game:GetService("ServerStorage")

local ApplyPropMeshes = {}

local SIZE_TOLERANCE = 0.02 -- relative: axis ratios (import size / data size) must agree within this
local ROTATION_TOLERANCE = 2 -- degrees: an imported mesh turned further than this is refused
local LAYOUT_TOLERANCE = 0.05 -- studs (or 0.4 % of the prop's size): relative position error allowed per mesh
local PREVIEW_ATTRIBUTE = "MapPropPreview" -- set on a template built from preview images
local HOLD = "_PreviewHold" -- MapProps._PreviewHold.<propId>: the untouched originals during a preview
local IMPORTED = "ImportedProps" -- ServerStorage.ImportedProps: the applied imports (sources of later runs)

local rgb3 = Color3.fromRGB
-- recoloured placements (attribute Variant on the instance): SurfaceAppearance.Color per mesh (README section 12),
-- = the old recolour's colour / the ColorMap mean. Used when the template has no _Variants of its own.
ApplyPropMeshes.VARIANTS = {
	rowboat = { -- Abyss_2: dark wet wood, rusty iron
		Sunken = {
			Hull = rgb3(111, 86, 71), Timber = rgb3(93, 71, 60), Thwarts = rgb3(91, 70, 59), Iron = rgb3(73, 82, 80),
			Rope = rgb3(125, 111, 89), Oar = rgb3(84, 66, 54), OarBlade = rgb3(90, 70, 58),
		},
	},
	skull_bones = { -- Abyss_3: bleached grey-green bones (sockets kept darker than today's pale ones so the skull reads)
		Pale = { Bones = rgb3(228, 234, 228), Aged = rgb3(215, 222, 215), Sockets = rgb3(126, 137, 137) },
	},
}
-- attributes the new model must not inherit from the instance it replaces (SyncMapProps MapPropDropAttributes)
-- (only the provenance attributes of a Toolbox mesh the Blender model fully replaces; every other attribute stays)
ApplyPropMeshes.DROP_ATTRIBUTES = {
	egg_nest = "SourceAssetId,SourceCreator", -- the Toolbox rock is gone: the new rock is ours
	minecart = "SourceAssetId,SourceCreator", -- the Toolbox cart meshes are gone too
}
-- "pieces only" props: the frame template's parts the Blender pieces replace (= the data Replaces: awning stripes
-- "Awning" x7 + fringe blocks "AwningFringe" x7, then the display items), and the ones a data collider takes over
ApplyPropMeshes.PIECES = {
	weapon_stall = {
		Remove = { "Awning", "AwningFringe", "SwordBlade", "SwordGuard", "SwordGrip", "Shield", "ShieldBoss", "AxeHandle", "AxeHead", "DisplaySword" },
		DataColliders = { Awning = true },
	},
	trophy_stall = {
		Remove = { "Awning", "AwningFringe", "TrophyCup", "CounterSkull" },
		DataColliders = { Awning = true },
	},
	diamond_shop = {
		Remove = { "Awning", "AwningFringe", "Diamond", "DiamondGirdle", "SignBar", "SignPost", "Cushion", "Gem" },
		DataColliders = { Awning = true },
	},
}
local PIECES_ROOT = "PiecesRoot"
local BASE = "_Base" -- MapProps._Base.<propId>: the frame template a pieces prop is built from

local function fresh(module: Instance): any
	local copy = module:Clone()
	copy.Parent = module.Parent
	local ok, result = pcall(require, copy)
	copy:Destroy()
	assert(ok, result)
	return result
end

local function devTool(name: string): Instance
	local tool = ServerStorage:FindFirstChild("DevTools") and ServerStorage.DevTools:FindFirstChild(name)
	assert(tool, `ServerStorage.DevTools.{name} is missing` .. (if name == "PropMeshData" then " (paste Blender_Exports/Props/PropMeshData.luau into it)" else ""))
	return tool :: Instance
end

local function v3(t: { number }): Vector3
	return Vector3.new(t[1], t[2], t[3])
end

local function rgb(t: { number }): Color3
	return Color3.fromRGB(t[1], t[2], t[3])
end

local function templateFolder(): Folder
	local folder = ServerStorage:FindFirstChild("MapProps")
	if not folder then
		folder = Instance.new("Folder")
		folder.Name = "MapProps"
		folder.Parent = ServerStorage
	end
	return folder :: Folder
end

-- the imported Model of a prop: top of the Workspace, Workspace.ImportedProps or ServerStorage.ImportedProps
-- (the map folders are never searched)
local function findImport(propId: string): Model?
	-- (the Workspace first: a new import wins over the stored one)
	local places: { Instance } = { workspace }
	local inWorkspace = workspace:FindFirstChild(IMPORTED)
	if inWorkspace then
		table.insert(places, inWorkspace)
	end
	local stored = ServerStorage:FindFirstChild(IMPORTED)
	if stored then
		table.insert(places, stored)
	end
	for _, place in ipairs(places) do
		for _, item in ipairs(place:GetChildren()) do
			if item:IsA("Model") and not item:HasTag("MapProp") then
				local name = string.gsub(string.lower(item.Name), "%.fbx$", "")
				if (string.match(name, "^%d%d_(.+)$") or name) == propId then
					return item
				end
			end
		end
	end
	return nil
end

local function setContent(inst: Instance, property: string, uri: string?)
	if not uri or uri == "" then
		return
	end
	local ok = pcall(function()
		(inst :: any)[property] = uri
	end)
	if not ok then
		pcall(function()
			(inst :: any)[property .. "Content"] = Content.fromUri(uri)
		end)
	end
end

local function surfaceFor(data: any, family: any, tint: Color3): SurfaceAppearance?
	local set = family.Set and data.Textures[family.Set]
	if not set then
		return nil
	end
	local sa = Instance.new("SurfaceAppearance")
	sa.Name = "SurfaceAppearance"
	setContent(sa, "ColorMap", set.ColorMap)
	setContent(sa, "NormalMap", set.NormalMap)
	setContent(sa, "RoughnessMap", family.RoughnessMap or set.RoughnessMap)
	setContent(sa, "MetalnessMap", set.MetalnessMap)
	pcall(function()
		sa.AlphaMode = Enum.AlphaMode.Overlay
	end)
	pcall(function()
		(sa :: any).Color = tint
	end)
	return sa
end

local function roleOf(name: string, info: any): string
	if info.Role and info.Role ~= "" then
		return info.Role
	end
	for _, role in ipairs({ "Glow", "Water", "Glass", "Stream", "Foam" }) do
		if string.find(name, "_" .. role .. "$") then
			return role
		end
	end
	return "Solid"
end

local function stripped(propId: string, name: string): string
	return (string.gsub(name, "^" .. propId .. "_", ""))
end

local function invisibleCollider(p: BasePart)
	p.Transparency = 1
	p.Anchored = true
	p.CanCollide = true
	p.CanQuery = true
	p.CanTouch = false
	p.CastShadow = false
end

local function material(name: string?, default: string): Enum.Material
	local ok, value = pcall(function()
		return (Enum.Material :: any)[name or default]
	end)
	return if ok and value then value else (Enum.Material :: any)[default]
end

-- the water_ripple overlay ("Ripples" Textures; Controllers/PropFX scrolls them)
local SIDES = { Enum.NormalId.Front, Enum.NormalId.Back, Enum.NormalId.Left, Enum.NormalId.Right }
local function ripples(mp: BasePart, data: any, overlayName: string?, faces: { Enum.NormalId })
	local overlay = overlayName and data.Textures[overlayName]
	if not overlay then
		return
	end
	for _, face in ipairs(faces) do
		local tex = Instance.new("Texture")
		tex.Name = "Ripples"
		tex.Face = face
		tex.Texture = overlay.ColorMap
		tex.StudsPerTileU = data.StudsPerTile or 4
		tex.StudsPerTileV = data.StudsPerTile or 4
		tex.Parent = mp
	end
end

-- the axes a size check can trust (thin axes are left out: a flat plane's thickness is not meaningful)
local function checkedAxes(want: Vector3): { string }
	local axes = {}
	for _, axis in ipairs({ "X", "Y", "Z" }) do
		if (want :: any)[axis] >= 0.2 then
			table.insert(axes, axis)
		end
	end
	if #axes == 0 then
		for _, axis in ipairs({ "X", "Y", "Z" }) do
			if (want :: any)[axis] > 0.01 then
				table.insert(axes, axis)
			end
		end
	end
	return axes
end

local function fmtV(v: Vector3): string
	return string.format("%.3f x %.3f x %.3f", v.X, v.Y, v.Z)
end

-- the import's meshes against the data (see the header). Returns ok, the problems (why it is skipped) and notes.
-- opts.standIn: collider meshes may be missing (the preview PNGs never hold them); opts.allowMissing: missing and
-- unknown meshes are only reported
local function validate(propId: string, prop: any, source: Instance, opts: any): (boolean, { string }, { string })
	local problems, notes = {}, {}
	local byName: { [string]: MeshPart } = {}
	local dupes = {}
	for _, d in ipairs(source:GetDescendants()) do
		if d:IsA("MeshPart") then
			if byName[d.Name] then
				table.insert(dupes, d.Name)
			else
				byName[d.Name] = d
			end
		end
	end
	local missing, extra = {}, {}
	for meshName, info in pairs(prop.Meshes) do
		if not byName[meshName] and not (opts.standIn and roleOf(meshName, info) == "Collider") then
			table.insert(missing, meshName)
		end
	end
	for name in pairs(byName) do
		if not prop.Meshes[name] then
			table.insert(extra, name)
		end
	end
	table.sort(missing)
	table.sort(extra)
	if #dupes > 0 then
		table.sort(dupes)
		table.insert(problems, "two meshes share a name: " .. table.concat(dupes, ", "))
	end
	local partial = {}
	if #missing > 0 then
		table.insert(partial, "missing meshes: " .. table.concat(missing, ", "))
	end
	if #extra > 0 then
		table.insert(partial, "meshes the data does not know (Merge Meshes ON? another file?): " .. table.concat(extra, ", "))
	end
	for _, text in ipairs(partial) do
		table.insert(if opts.allowMissing then notes else problems, text)
	end
	-- rotation and size: one common factor for every mesh
	local found = {}
	for meshName, info in pairs(prop.Meshes) do
		local src = byName[meshName]
		if not src then
			continue
		end
		local _, angle = src.CFrame.Rotation:ToAxisAngle()
		if math.deg(math.abs(angle)) > ROTATION_TOLERANCE then
			local rx, ry, rz = src.CFrame:ToOrientation()
			table.insert(problems, string.format("%s is rotated (%.0f, %.0f, %.0f deg): re-import with World Forward = Front, World Up = Top", meshName, math.deg(rx), math.deg(ry), math.deg(rz)))
			continue
		end
		local want = v3(info.Size)
		local lo, hi = math.huge, -math.huge
		for _, axis in ipairs(checkedAxes(want)) do
			local r = (src.Size :: any)[axis] / (want :: any)[axis]
			lo, hi = math.min(lo, r), math.max(hi, r)
		end
		if lo <= 0 or hi / lo - 1 > SIZE_TOLERANCE then
			table.insert(problems, `{meshName}: size {fmtV(src.Size)} is not its data size {fmtV(want)} scaled evenly (distorted or turned)`)
			continue
		end
		table.insert(found, { name = meshName, src = src, factor = (lo + hi) / 2, center = v3(info.Center) })
	end
	if #found == 0 then
		if #problems == 0 then
			table.insert(problems, "no mesh of the data found")
		end
		return false, problems, notes
	end
	local factors = {}
	for _, f in ipairs(found) do
		table.insert(factors, f.factor)
	end
	table.sort(factors)
	local k = factors[(#factors + 1) // 2]
	for _, f in ipairs(found) do
		if math.abs(f.factor / k - 1) > SIZE_TOLERANCE then
			table.insert(problems, string.format("%s is scaled x%.3f, the other meshes x%.3f", f.name, f.factor, k))
		end
	end
	if math.abs(k - 1) > SIZE_TOLERANCE then
		table.insert(notes, string.format("import unit off by x%.3f (Scale Unit not Studs?): every mesh resized to its data size", k))
	end
	-- layout: the positions relative to each other (expected: k * Center + one common offset)
	if #found >= 2 then
		local offset = Vector3.zero
		for _, f in ipairs(found) do
			offset += f.src.Position - f.center * k
		end
		offset /= #found
		local b = prop.Bounds and v3(prop.Bounds.Size) or Vector3.one
		local tol = k * math.max(LAYOUT_TOLERANCE, 0.004 * b.Magnitude)
		local worst, worstName = 0, ""
		for _, f in ipairs(found) do
			local err = (f.src.Position - f.center * k - offset).Magnitude
			if err > worst then
				worst, worstName = err, f.name
			end
		end
		if worst > tol then
			table.insert(problems, string.format("layout: %s is %.2f studs off its place relative to the other meshes (allowed %.2f): a turned, mirrored or edited import", worstName, worst, tol))
		end
	end
	return #problems == 0, problems, notes
end
ApplyPropMeshes.validate = validate

-- one render MeshPart (a clone of the import / preview mesh, already validated) -> its template look; placed by the
-- caller
local function dress(mp: MeshPart, propId: string, meshName: string, info: any, data: any)
	for _, child in ipairs(mp:GetChildren()) do
		child:Destroy() -- imported SurfaceAppearance / welds: replaced below
	end
	mp.Size = v3(info.Size) -- (validated: equal, or off by the common import factor)
	mp.Anchored = true
	mp.CanCollide = false
	mp.CanTouch = false
	mp.CanQuery = false
	mp.CastShadow = info.CastShadow == true
	pcall(function()
		mp.CollisionFidelity = Enum.CollisionFidelity.Box
	end)
	local center = v3(info.Center)
	mp.PivotOffset = CFrame.new(v3(info.Pivot or { 0, 0, 0 }) - center)
	local tint = rgb(info.Color)
	local role = roleOf(meshName, info)
	local family = data.Families[info.Family] or {}
	mp.Color = tint
	mp.Transparency = info.Transparency or 0
	if role == "Glow" then
		mp.Material = Enum.Material.Neon
	elseif role == "Water" or role == "Glass" or role == "Stream" then
		mp.Material = material(info.Material or family.Material, "Glass")
		mp.Transparency = info.Transparency or family.Transparency or (if role == "Water" then 0.35 elseif role == "Stream" then 0.45 else 0.3)
		if role == "Water" then
			ripples(mp, data, info.Overlay or family.Overlay, { Enum.NormalId.Top })
		elseif role == "Stream" then
			ripples(mp, data, info.Overlay or family.Overlay, SIDES)
		end
	elseif role == "Foam" then
		mp.Material = material(info.Material or family.Material, "SmoothPlastic")
		mp.Transparency = info.Transparency or family.Transparency or 0.2
	else
		mp.Material = material(info.Material or family.Material, "SmoothPlastic")
		local sa = surfaceFor(data, family, tint)
		if sa then
			sa.Parent = mp
		end
	end
	mp.Name = stripped(propId, meshName)
end

-- a collider mesh (Role "Collider"): the imported Hull mesh, or (preview) a stand-in box of its data size
local function colliderMesh(propId: string, meshName: string, info: any, src: MeshPart?, at: CFrame, model: Model, opts: any, notes: { string })
	if src then
		local cm = src:Clone()
		for _, child in ipairs(cm:GetChildren()) do
			child:Destroy()
		end
		cm.Size = v3(info.Size) -- (validated like the render meshes)
		invisibleCollider(cm)
		pcall(function()
			cm.CollisionFidelity = Enum.CollisionFidelity.Hull
		end)
		cm.CFrame = at
		cm.Name = stripped(propId, meshName)
		cm.Parent = model
	elseif opts.standIn then
		local box = Instance.new("Part")
		box.Name = stripped(propId, meshName)
		box.Size = v3(info.Size)
		box.CFrame = at
		invisibleCollider(box)
		box:SetAttribute("PreviewStandIn", true)
		box.Parent = model
		table.insert(notes, `{meshName}: preview stand-in box {box.Size.X} x {box.Size.Y} x {box.Size.Z} (the import brings the Hull mesh)`)
	else
		table.insert(notes, `collider mesh {meshName} missing`)
	end
end

-- the data colliders (invisible simple parts)
local function addColliders(model: Model, propId: string, prop: any, pivot: CFrame)
	for _, c in ipairs(prop.Colliders or {}) do
		local p: BasePart
		if c.Shape == "Wedge" then
			p = Instance.new("WedgePart")
		else
			local part = Instance.new("Part")
			part.Shape = if c.Shape == "Cylinder" then Enum.PartType.Cylinder
				elseif c.Shape == "Ball" then Enum.PartType.Ball
				else Enum.PartType.Block
			p = part
		end
		local r = c.Rotation or { 0, 0, 0 }
		p.Name = stripped(propId, c.Name)
		p.Size = v3(c.Size)
		p.CFrame = pivot * CFrame.new(v3(c.Center)) * CFrame.fromOrientation(math.rad(r[1]), math.rad(r[2]), math.rad(r[3]))
		invisibleCollider(p)
		p.Parent = model
	end
end

local function attachmentNamed(model: Instance, name: string): Attachment?
	for _, d in ipairs(model:GetDescendants()) do
		if d:IsA("Attachment") and d.Name == name then
			return d
		end
	end
	return nil
end

-- one Config/PropFX Particles spec -> a ParticleEmitter (off; Controllers/PropFX runs it near the player)
local function emitter(spec: any): ParticleEmitter
	local pe = Instance.new("ParticleEmitter")
	pe.Name = "PropFX_" .. spec.Attachment
	pe.Enabled = false
	if spec.Texture then
		pe.Texture = spec.Texture
	end
	pe.Color = ColorSequence.new(spec.Color)
	pe.Rate = spec.Rate
	pe.Lifetime = NumberRange.new(spec.Lifetime[1], spec.Lifetime[2])
	if spec.SizeEnd then
		pe.Size = NumberSequence.new(spec.Size, spec.SizeEnd)
	else
		pe.Size = NumberSequence.new({ NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0, 0), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(0.3, spec.Size), NumberSequenceKeypoint.new(1, 0) })
	end
	if spec.Transparency then
		pe.Transparency = NumberSequence.new(spec.Transparency[1], spec.Transparency[2])
	end
	local speed = spec.Speed or 0
	pe.Speed = if type(speed) == "table" then NumberRange.new(speed[1], speed[2]) else NumberRange.new(speed)
	local spread = spec.Spread or 180
	pe.SpreadAngle = Vector2.new(spread, spread)
	if spec.Acceleration then
		pe.Acceleration = v3(spec.Acceleration)
	end
	pe.Drag = spec.Drag or 0
	pe.LightEmission = spec.LightEmission or 1
	if spec.LightInfluence then
		pe.LightInfluence = spec.LightInfluence
	end
	pe.Rotation = NumberRange.new(0, 360)
	if spec.RotSpeed then
		pe.RotSpeed = NumberRange.new(-spec.RotSpeed, spec.RotSpeed)
	end
	return pe
end

-- the data Attachments under fxRoot (moveOf(position) = the re-basing of the item an attachment sits in), then the
-- PropFX static lights and particle emitters
local function addEffects(model: Model, fxRoot: BasePart, prop: any, pivot: CFrame, entry: any, notes: { string }, moveOf: ((Vector3) -> CFrame)?)
	for name, pos in pairs(prop.Attachments or {}) do
		local att = Instance.new("Attachment")
		att.Name = name
		local at = pivot * CFrame.new(v3(pos))
		if moveOf then
			at = moveOf(v3(pos)) * at
		end
		att.CFrame = fxRoot.CFrame:ToObjectSpace(at)
		att.Parent = fxRoot
	end
	for _, spec in ipairs(entry and entry.Lights or {}) do
		-- on an Attachment, or on the part "<Part>" / the Blender glow name "<Part>_Glow"
		local host: Instance? = if spec.Attachment then attachmentNamed(model, spec.Attachment)
			else model:FindFirstChild(spec.Part, true) or model:FindFirstChild(spec.Part .. "_Glow", true)
		if host and (host:IsA("BasePart") or host:IsA("Attachment")) then
			local light = Instance.new("PointLight")
			light.Color, light.Brightness, light.Range, light.Shadows = spec.Color, spec.Brightness, spec.Range, false
			light.Parent = host
		else
			table.insert(notes, `light host "{spec.Attachment or spec.Part}" missing`)
		end
	end
	for _, spec in ipairs(entry and entry.Particles or {}) do
		local att = fxRoot:FindFirstChild(spec.Attachment)
		if att then
			emitter(spec).Parent = att
		else
			table.insert(notes, `particle attachment "{spec.Attachment}" missing`)
		end
	end
end

-- the part named `name` (of size `size` when some are) nearest to `at`, among the direct children of `model`
local function partNear(model: Instance, name: string, at: Vector3, size: Vector3?): (BasePart?, number)
	local candidates = {}
	for _, c in ipairs(model:GetChildren()) do
		if c:IsA("BasePart") and c.Name == name then
			table.insert(candidates, c)
		end
	end
	if size then
		local fit = {}
		for _, c in ipairs(candidates) do
			if (c.Size - size).Magnitude < 0.05 then
				table.insert(fit, c)
			end
		end
		if #fit > 0 then
			candidates = fit
		end
	end
	local best, bestD = nil, math.huge
	for _, c in ipairs(candidates) do
		local d = (c.Position - at).Magnitude
		if d < bestD then
			best, bestD = c, d
		end
	end
	return best, bestD
end

-- the source's MeshParts by name (the first of a name; validate() refuses duplicates)
local function meshesByName(source: Instance): { [string]: MeshPart }
	local byName: { [string]: MeshPart } = {}
	for _, d in ipairs(source:GetDescendants()) do
		if d:IsA("MeshPart") and not byName[d.Name] then
			byName[d.Name] = d
		end
	end
	return byName
end

-- builds the template Model from a source Model holding MeshParts named like the data meshes. Returns nil and the
-- reasons when validate() refuses the source.
-- opts.standIn: a collider MESH (Role "Collider") missing from the source (the preview PNGs never hold them) becomes
-- an invisible box of its data Size (attribute PreviewStandIn); opts.allowMissing: see validate()
local function build(propId: string, source: Instance, data: any, propFx: any, opts: any?): (Model?, { string })
	opts = opts or {}
	local prop = data.Props[propId]
	if not prop then
		return nil, { `no PropMeshData entry for {propId}` }
	end
	local ok, problems, notes = validate(propId, prop, source, opts)
	if not ok then
		return nil, problems
	end
	-- 1. the meshes by their data names (before they are renamed <Part>)
	local byName = meshesByName(source)
	local model = Instance.new("Model")
	model.Name = propId
	local bounds = prop.Bounds
	local root = Instance.new("Part")
	root.Name = "Root"
	root.Size = v3(bounds.Size)
	root.CFrame = CFrame.new(v3(bounds.Center))
	root.Transparency = 1
	root.Anchored = true
	root.CanCollide = false
	root.CanQuery = false
	root.CanTouch = false
	root.CastShadow = false
	root.Parent = model
	local pivot = CFrame.new(0, prop.PivotY or 0, 0)
	for meshName, info in pairs(prop.Meshes) do
		local src = byName[meshName]
		if roleOf(meshName, info) == "Collider" then
			-- convex collision mesh: invisible Hull collider, never rendered
			colliderMesh(propId, meshName, info, src, pivot * CFrame.new(v3(info.Center)), model, opts, notes)
			continue
		end
		if not src then
			continue -- (only with opts.allowMissing; reported by validate)
		end
		local mp = src:Clone()
		dress(mp, propId, meshName, info, data)
		mp.CFrame = pivot * CFrame.new(v3(info.Center))
		mp.Parent = model
	end
	addColliders(model, propId, prop, pivot)
	-- effect points, static lights, particle emitters (off: Controllers/PropFX turns them on near the player)
	addEffects(model, root, prop, pivot, propFx and propFx.Props[propId], notes, nil)
	model.PrimaryPart = root
	root.PivotOffset = root.CFrame:ToObjectSpace(pivot)
	model:SetAttribute("MapPropId", propId)
	if ApplyPropMeshes.DROP_ATTRIBUTES[propId] then
		model:SetAttribute("MapPropDropAttributes", ApplyPropMeshes.DROP_ATTRIBUTES[propId])
	end
	local variants = ApplyPropMeshes.VARIANTS[propId]
	if variants then
		local folder = Instance.new("Folder")
		folder.Name = "_Variants"
		for variantName, colors in pairs(variants) do
			local config = Instance.new("Configuration")
			config.Name = variantName
			for partName, color in pairs(colors) do
				config:SetAttribute("Color_" .. partName, color)
			end
			config.Parent = folder
		end
		folder.Parent = model
	end
	return model, notes
end
ApplyPropMeshes.build = build

-- the frame template a pieces prop starts from: MapProps._Base.<propId> (saved by the first real run), else the
-- current template when it is the bare Studio-built frame
local function piecesBase(propId: string): (Model?, string?)
	local folder = templateFolder()
	local saved = folder:FindFirstChild(BASE) and folder[BASE]:FindFirstChild(propId)
	if saved and saved:IsA("Model") then
		return saved, nil
	end
	local current = folder:FindFirstChild(propId)
	if not current or not current:IsA("Model") then
		return nil, `no frame template MapProps.{propId} (Studio-built, StudioProps)`
	end
	if current:GetAttribute(PREVIEW_ATTRIBUTE) then
		return nil, `a preview is installed: run endPreview("{propId}") first`
	end
	if current:GetAttribute("MapPropPieces") then
		return nil, `the pieces are already in MapProps.{propId} and MapProps.{BASE}.{propId} is missing`
	end
	return current, nil
end

local function savePiecesBase(propId: string, base: Model)
	local folder = templateFolder()
	local store = folder:FindFirstChild(BASE) or Instance.new("Folder")
	store.Name = BASE
	store.Parent = folder
	if not store:FindFirstChild(propId) then
		local copy = base:Clone()
		copy.Parent = store
	end
end

-- a "pieces only" prop: the Blender pieces in a copy of the frame template (see the header)
local function buildPieces(propId: string, source: Instance, data: any, propFx: any, base: Model, opts: any?): (Model?, { string })
	opts = opts or {}
	local prop = data.Props[propId]
	local spec = ApplyPropMeshes.PIECES[propId]
	if not prop then
		return nil, { `no PropMeshData entry for {propId}` }
	end
	local ok, problems, notes = validate(propId, prop, source, opts)
	if not ok then
		return nil, problems
	end
	local byName = meshesByName(source)
	local model = base:Clone()
	model.Name = propId
	for _, key in ipairs({ "MapPropVersion", PREVIEW_ATTRIBUTE, "MapPropPieces" }) do
		model:SetAttribute(key, nil)
	end
	local oldRoot = model:FindFirstChild(PIECES_ROOT)
	if oldRoot then
		oldRoot:Destroy()
	end
	local pivot = model:GetPivot()
	-- 1. anchors, found on the frame's parts before anything leaves
	local moves: { [string]: CFrame } = {}
	local anchored: { { lo: Vector3, hi: Vector3, move: CFrame, volume: number } } = {}
	local seenAnchor: { [string]: boolean } = {}
	for meshName, info in pairs(prop.Meshes) do
		local a = info.Anchor
		if a then
			local r = a.AssumedRotation or { 0, 0, 0 }
			local assumed = pivot * CFrame.new(v3(a.AssumedPosition)) * CFrame.fromOrientation(math.rad(r[1]), math.rad(r[2]), math.rad(r[3]))
			local real, dist = partNear(model, a.Part, assumed.Position, if a.PartSize then v3(a.PartSize) else nil)
			if real then
				local move = real.CFrame * assumed:Inverse()
				moves[meshName] = move
				local half = v3(info.Size) / 2 + Vector3.one * 0.6
				local c = v3(info.Center)
				table.insert(anchored, { lo = c - half, hi = c + half, move = move, volume = info.Size[1] * info.Size[2] * info.Size[3] })
				local key = `{a.Part}@{a.AssumedPosition[1]},{a.AssumedPosition[2]},{a.AssumedPosition[3]}`
				if not seenAnchor[key] then
					seenAnchor[key] = true
					local rp = pivot:PointToObjectSpace(real.Position)
					local rx, ry, rz = pivot:ToObjectSpace(real.CFrame):ToOrientation()
					table.insert(notes, string.format("anchor %s: assumed (%.2f, %.2f, %.2f) rot (%g, %g, %g) -> real (%.2f, %.2f, %.2f) rot (%.0f, %.0f, %.0f), %.2f away",
						a.Part, a.AssumedPosition[1], a.AssumedPosition[2], a.AssumedPosition[3], r[1], r[2], r[3], rp.X, rp.Y, rp.Z, math.deg(rx), math.deg(ry), math.deg(rz), dist))
				end
			else
				table.insert(notes, `anchor part "{a.Part}" of {meshName} not found: placed as modelled`)
			end
		end
	end
	-- 2. the replaced frame parts (solid ones stay as invisible colliders unless a data collider takes over)
	local remove: { [string]: boolean } = {}
	for _, name in ipairs(spec.Remove) do
		remove[name] = true
	end
	local gone, solid = 0, 0
	local found: { [string]: number } = {}
	for _, c in ipairs(model:GetChildren()) do
		if c:IsA("BasePart") and remove[c.Name] then
			found[c.Name] = (found[c.Name] or 0) + 1
			if c.CanCollide and not (spec.DataColliders and spec.DataColliders[c.Name]) then
				for _, child in ipairs(c:GetChildren()) do
					child:Destroy()
				end
				c.Name = "Collider_" .. c.Name
				invisibleCollider(c)
				solid += 1
			else
				c:Destroy()
				gone += 1
			end
		end
	end
	local counts = {}
	for _, name in ipairs(spec.Remove) do
		table.insert(counts, `{name} x{found[name] or 0}`)
	end
	table.insert(notes, `replaced frame parts: {table.concat(counts, ", ")} ({gone} removed, {solid} kept as invisible colliders)`)
	-- 3. the meshes
	for meshName, info in pairs(prop.Meshes) do
		local src = byName[meshName]
		local at = (moves[meshName] or CFrame.identity) * pivot * CFrame.new(v3(info.Center))
		if roleOf(meshName, info) == "Collider" then
			colliderMesh(propId, meshName, info, src, at, model, opts, notes)
			continue
		end
		if not src then
			continue -- (only with opts.allowMissing; reported by validate)
		end
		local mp = src:Clone()
		dress(mp, propId, meshName, info, data)
		mp.CFrame = at
		mp.Parent = model
	end
	-- 4. data colliders, effects root, attachments (re-based with the smallest anchored item holding them)
	addColliders(model, propId, prop, pivot)
	local fxRoot = Instance.new("Part")
	fxRoot.Name = PIECES_ROOT
	fxRoot.Size = Vector3.one
	fxRoot.CFrame = pivot * CFrame.new(v3(prop.Bounds.Center))
	fxRoot.Transparency = 1
	fxRoot.Anchored = true
	fxRoot.CanCollide = false
	fxRoot.CanQuery = false
	fxRoot.CanTouch = false
	fxRoot.CastShadow = false
	fxRoot.Parent = model
	local function moveOf(pos: Vector3): CFrame
		local best, volume = CFrame.identity, math.huge
		for _, item in ipairs(anchored) do
			if pos.X >= item.lo.X and pos.X <= item.hi.X and pos.Y >= item.lo.Y and pos.Y <= item.hi.Y and pos.Z >= item.lo.Z and pos.Z <= item.hi.Z and item.volume < volume then
				best, volume = item.move, item.volume
			end
		end
		return best
	end
	addEffects(model, fxRoot, prop, pivot, propFx and propFx.Props[propId], notes, moveOf)
	model:SetAttribute("MapPropId", propId)
	model:SetAttribute("MapPropPieces", true)
	return model, notes
end
ApplyPropMeshes.buildPieces = buildPieces

-- nested props (data Placement.OriginInHost): the offset of every nested instance in its host, against the data
local function placementCheck(propId: string, prop: any): string?
	local placement = prop and prop.Placement
	if not placement or not placement.OriginInHost then
		return nil
	end
	local want = v3(placement.OriginInHost)
	local wantRot = placement.RotationInHost or { 0, 0, 0 }
	local ok, bad = 0, {}
	for _, inst in ipairs(CollectionService:GetTagged("MapProp")) do
		if inst:IsA("Model") and inst:GetAttribute("MapPropId") == propId and inst.Parent and inst.Parent:IsA("Model") and inst.Parent:GetAttribute("MapPropId") then
			local rel = (inst.Parent :: Model):GetPivot():ToObjectSpace(inst:GetPivot())
			local _, ry = rel:ToOrientation()
			if (rel.Position - want).Magnitude < 0.01 and math.abs(math.deg(ry) - wantRot[2]) < 0.1 then
				ok += 1
			else
				table.insert(bad, string.format("%s at (%.3f, %.3f, %.3f) yaw %.1f", inst:GetFullName(), rel.X, rel.Y, rel.Z, math.deg(ry)))
			end
		end
	end
	if ok == 0 and #bad == 0 then
		return nil -- a top-level prop (the stalls: Placement without nesting)
	end
	return `nested in the host at OriginInHost ({want.X}, {want.Y}, {want.Z}): {ok} ok` .. (if #bad > 0 then "; OFF: " .. table.concat(bad, "; ") else "")
end

-- a template keeps the recolour variants of the one it replaces when it has none of its own
local function inheritVariants(model: Model, old: Instance?)
	local variants = old and old:FindFirstChild("_Variants")
	if variants and not model:FindFirstChild("_Variants") then
		variants:Clone().Parent = model
	end
end

-- is a preview of propId installed (its template, or its held originals)?
local function previewBusy(propId: string): boolean
	local folder = templateFolder()
	local current = folder:FindFirstChild(propId)
	local hold = folder:FindFirstChild(HOLD)
	return (current ~= nil and current:GetAttribute(PREVIEW_ATTRIBUTE) ~= nil) or (hold ~= nil and hold:FindFirstChild(propId) ~= nil)
end

-- the applied import goes to ServerStorage.ImportedProps (an older import of the same name to _Replaced)
local function stashImport(import: Instance): string
	local store = ServerStorage:FindFirstChild(IMPORTED)
	if not store then
		store = Instance.new("Folder")
		store.Name = IMPORTED
		store.Parent = ServerStorage
	end
	if import.Parent == store then
		return import:GetFullName()
	end
	local older = store:FindFirstChild(import.Name)
	if older then
		local replaced = store:FindFirstChild("_Replaced") or Instance.new("Folder")
		replaced.Name = "_Replaced"
		replaced.Parent = store
		older.Parent = replaced
	end
	import.Parent = store
	return import:GetFullName()
end

-- CollisionFidelity only takes effect on a part in the Workspace (asynchronously): the new template visits a stage
-- far from the map until its meshes have it (colliding collider meshes Hull, render meshes Box), then comes back to
-- the origin. Returns a note when some part did not take it within 10 s.
local function settleFidelity(model: Model): string?
	local want: { [MeshPart]: Enum.CollisionFidelity } = {}
	local count = 0
	for _, d in ipairs(model:GetDescendants()) do
		if d:IsA("MeshPart") then
			want[d] = if d.CanCollide then Enum.CollisionFidelity.Hull else Enum.CollisionFidelity.Box
			count += 1
		end
	end
	if count == 0 then
		return nil
	end
	local home = model:GetPivot()
	local stage = Instance.new("Folder")
	stage.Name = "_ApplyPropMeshesStage"
	model:PivotTo(CFrame.new(0, 1000, 60000))
	model.Parent = stage
	stage.Parent = workspace
	for part, fidelity in pairs(want) do
		pcall(function()
			part.CollisionFidelity = fidelity
		end)
	end
	local deadline = os.clock() + 10
	local late = {}
	repeat
		task.wait(0.1)
		table.clear(late)
		for part, fidelity in pairs(want) do
			if part.CollisionFidelity ~= fidelity then
				table.insert(late, part.Name)
			end
		end
	until #late == 0 or os.clock() > deadline
	model.Parent = nil
	model:PivotTo(home)
	stage:Destroy()
	if #late > 0 then
		table.sort(late)
		return "CollisionFidelity not applied on " .. table.concat(late, ", ")
	end
	return nil
end

-- puts a template in ServerStorage.MapProps (the old one, with its _Variants copied over, goes to _Previous)
local function install(propId: string, model: Model)
	local folder = templateFolder()
	local old = folder:FindFirstChild(propId)
	if old then
		inheritVariants(model, old)
		local previous = folder:FindFirstChild("_Previous") or Instance.new("Folder")
		previous.Name = "_Previous"
		previous.Parent = folder
		local stale = previous:FindFirstChild(propId)
		if stale then
			stale:Destroy()
		end
		old.Parent = previous
	end
	model.Parent = folder
end

-- opts: only = { propId }, dryRun (report only), allowMissing (accept missing / unknown meshes), data (tests: a
-- PropMeshData table instead of DevTools.PropMeshData)
function ApplyPropMeshes.run(opts: any?): string
	opts = opts or {}
	local data = opts.data or fresh(devTool("PropMeshData"))
	local Sync = fresh(devTool("SyncMapProps"))
	local propFx = fresh(ReplicatedStorage.GameSystem.Config.PropFX)
	local ids = opts.only
	if not ids then
		ids = {}
		for id in pairs(data.Props) do
			table.insert(ids, id)
		end
		table.sort(ids)
	end
	local lines, applied = { if opts.dryRun then "ApplyPropMeshes (DRY RUN, nothing changed)" else "ApplyPropMeshes" }, {}
	local buildOpts = { allowMissing = opts.allowMissing == true }
	for _, propId in ipairs(ids) do
		local import = findImport(propId)
		if not import then
			table.insert(lines, `{propId}: not imported yet (Blender_Exports/Props/{propId}.fbx)`)
			continue
		end
		if previewBusy(propId) then
			table.insert(lines, `{propId}: SKIPPED - a preview is installed: run endPreview("{propId}") first`)
			continue
		end
		local model, notes, base
		if ApplyPropMeshes.PIECES[propId] then
			local why
			base, why = piecesBase(propId)
			if not base then
				table.insert(lines, `{propId}: SKIPPED - {why}`)
				continue
			end
			model, notes = buildPieces(propId, import, data, propFx, base, buildOpts)
		else
			model, notes = build(propId, import, data, propFx, buildOpts)
		end
		if not model then
			-- today's template and models stay as they are
			table.insert(lines, `{propId}: SKIPPED, nothing changed ({import:GetFullName()}): ` .. table.concat(notes, "; "))
			continue
		end
		local check = placementCheck(propId, data.Props[propId])
		if check then
			table.insert(notes, check)
		end
		local fidelity = settleFidelity(model)
		if fidelity then
			table.insert(notes, fidelity)
		end
		local detail = if #notes > 0 then " - " .. table.concat(notes, "; ") else ""
		local folder = templateFolder()
		local current = folder:FindFirstChild(propId)
		inheritVariants(model, current)
		local same = current ~= nil and current:IsA("Model") and Sync.fingerprint(current :: Model) == Sync.fingerprint(model)
		if opts.dryRun then
			model:Destroy()
			table.insert(lines, `{propId}: would {if same then "keep (unchanged)" else "apply"} {import:GetFullName()}{detail}`)
			continue
		end
		if same then
			-- a second run with the same import: the template stays (and _Previous keeps the real previous one)
			model:Destroy()
			table.insert(lines, `{propId}: unchanged (MapProps.{propId} already holds this import); import kept in {stashImport(import)}`)
			continue
		end
		if base then
			savePiecesBase(propId, base) -- the next run starts from the same frame
		end
		install(propId, model)
		table.insert(applied, propId)
		local from = import:GetFullName()
		table.insert(lines, `{propId}: applied from {from}{detail}; import moved to {stashImport(import)}`)
		task.wait()
	end
	if #applied > 0 then
		table.insert(lines, Sync.run({ only = applied }))
	end
	return table.concat(lines, "\n")
end

---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Studio preview from the PNG-encoded meshes (Blender/Props/README.txt "Preview images", tools/blender/fyd_props.py)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
local function adler32(buf: buffer, from: number, len: number): number
	local a, b = 1, 0
	for i = from, from + len - 1 do
		a = (a + buffer.readu8(buf, i)) % 65521
		b = (b + a) % 65521
	end
	return b * 65536 + a
end

-- one image -> its decoded JSON table
local function decodeImage(imageId: string): (any?, string?)
	local ok, image = pcall(function()
		return AssetService:CreateEditableImageAsync(Content.fromUri(imageId))
	end)
	if not ok or not image then
		return nil, `cannot open {imageId}: {image}`
	end
	local size = image.Size
	local pixels = image:ReadPixelsBuffer(Vector2.zero, size)
	image:Destroy() -- free the EditableImage budget at once
	local count = size.X * size.Y
	local bytes = buffer.create(count * 3)
	for i = 0, count - 1 do
		buffer.writeu8(bytes, i * 3, buffer.readu8(pixels, i * 4))
		buffer.writeu8(bytes, i * 3 + 1, buffer.readu8(pixels, i * 4 + 1))
		buffer.writeu8(bytes, i * 3 + 2, buffer.readu8(pixels, i * 4 + 2))
	end
	if buffer.readstring(bytes, 0, 4) ~= "FYDM" then
		return nil, `{imageId}: bad magic (not a FYDM image, or the upload was not lossless)`
	end
	local length = buffer.readu32(bytes, 4)
	local sum = buffer.readu32(bytes, 8)
	if 12 + length > count * 3 then
		return nil, `{imageId}: JSON length {length} does not fit in the image`
	end
	local got = adler32(bytes, 12, length)
	if got ~= sum then
		return nil, string.format("%s: Adler-32 mismatch (%08x, expected %08x): the upload may not be lossless", imageId, got, sum)
	end
	local decoded, result = pcall(function()
		return HttpService:JSONDecode(buffer.readstring(bytes, 12, length))
	end)
	if not decoded then
		return nil, `{imageId}: JSON error {result}`
	end
	return result, nil
end

-- one decoded mesh -> a MeshPart named like the import would name it, placed in prop space (centred on its box)
local function meshPart(mesh: any): (MeshPart?, string?)
	local em = AssetService:CreateEditableMesh()
	local v, n, uv, c, t = mesh.v, mesh.n, mesh.uv, mesh.c, mesh.t
	local count = #v // 3
	local vid, nid, uid, cid = table.create(count), table.create(count), table.create(count), table.create(count)
	local mn, mx = Vector3.one * math.huge, -Vector3.one * math.huge
	for i = 0, count - 1 do
		local p = Vector3.new(v[i * 3 + 1], v[i * 3 + 2], v[i * 3 + 3])
		mn, mx = mn:Min(p), mx:Max(p)
	end
	local center = (mn + mx) / 2
	for i = 0, count - 1 do
		vid[i + 1] = em:AddVertex(Vector3.new(v[i * 3 + 1], v[i * 3 + 2], v[i * 3 + 3]) - center)
		if n then
			nid[i + 1] = em:AddNormal(Vector3.new(n[i * 3 + 1], n[i * 3 + 2], n[i * 3 + 3]))
		end
		if uv then
			uid[i + 1] = em:AddUV(Vector2.new(uv[i * 2 + 1], uv[i * 2 + 2]))
		end
		if c then
			cid[i + 1] = em:AddColor(Color3.fromRGB(c[i * 3 + 1], c[i * 3 + 2], c[i * 3 + 3]), 1)
		end
	end
	for f = 0, #t // 3 - 1 do
		local a, b, d = t[f * 3 + 1] + 1, t[f * 3 + 2] + 1, t[f * 3 + 3] + 1
		local face = em:AddTriangle(vid[a], vid[b], vid[d])
		if n then
			em:SetFaceNormals(face, { nid[a], nid[b], nid[d] })
		end
		if uv then
			em:SetFaceUVs(face, { uid[a], uid[b], uid[d] })
		end
		if c then
			em:SetFaceColors(face, { cid[a], cid[b], cid[d] })
		end
	end
	local ok, part = pcall(function()
		return AssetService:CreateMeshPartAsync(Content.fromObject(em))
	end)
	if not ok or not part then
		em:Destroy()
		return nil, `{mesh.name}: CreateMeshPartAsync failed: {part}`
	end
	part.Name = mesh.name
	part.Size = mx - mn
	part.CFrame = CFrame.new(center)
	part.Anchored = true
	return part, nil
end

-- decode the images into a Model like the FBX import, then the normal build + install + sync
function ApplyPropMeshes.preview(propId: string, imageIds: { string }): string
	local data = fresh(devTool("PropMeshData"))
	local Sync = fresh(devTool("SyncMapProps"))
	local propFx = fresh(ReplicatedStorage.GameSystem.Config.PropFX)
	local lines = { `ApplyPropMeshes.preview({propId}) - TEMPORARY, run endPreview("{propId}") before any save` }
	if previewBusy(propId) then
		-- a second preview would push the first one into _Previous and lose the real previous template
		table.insert(lines, `  REFUSED: a preview of {propId} is already installed: run endPreview("{propId}") first`)
		return table.concat(lines, "\n")
	end
	local source = Instance.new("Model")
	source.Name = propId
	local made = 0
	for _, id in ipairs(imageIds) do
		local decoded, err = decodeImage(id)
		if not decoded then
			table.insert(lines, "  FAILED " .. tostring(err))
			continue
		end
		if decoded.prop ~= propId then
			table.insert(lines, `  FAILED {id}: the image holds "{decoded.prop}"`)
			continue
		end
		for _, mesh in ipairs(decoded.meshes) do
			local part, perr = meshPart(mesh)
			if part then
				part.Parent = source
				made += 1
			else
				table.insert(lines, "  FAILED " .. tostring(perr))
			end
			task.wait()
		end
	end
	table.insert(lines, `  decoded {made} mesh(es) from {#imageIds} image(s)`)
	if made == 0 then
		source:Destroy()
		return table.concat(lines, "\n")
	end
	local model, notes
	if ApplyPropMeshes.PIECES[propId] then
		local base, why = piecesBase(propId)
		if not base then
			source:Destroy()
			table.insert(lines, "  SKIPPED: " .. tostring(why))
			return table.concat(lines, "\n")
		end
		model, notes = buildPieces(propId, source, data, propFx, base, { standIn = true })
	else
		model, notes = build(propId, source, data, propFx, { standIn = true })
	end
	source:Destroy() -- the template holds clones
	local check = placementCheck(propId, data.Props[propId])
	if check then
		table.insert(notes, check)
	end
	for _, note in ipairs(notes) do
		table.insert(lines, "  " .. note)
	end
	if not model then
		table.insert(lines, "  SKIPPED: no template built, nothing changed")
		return table.concat(lines, "\n")
	end
	model:SetAttribute(PREVIEW_ATTRIBUTE, true)
	-- keep the untouched originals in MapProps._PreviewHold.<propId> (a template area: never synced); a copy of each
	-- takes its place and is the one the sync replaces. endPreview puts the originals back exactly.
	local folder = templateFolder()
	local hold = folder:FindFirstChild(HOLD) or Instance.new("Folder")
	hold.Name = HOLD
	hold.Parent = folder
	local held = 0
	if not hold:FindFirstChild(propId) then
		local propHold = Instance.new("Folder")
		propHold.Name = propId
		propHold.Parent = hold
		for _, inst in ipairs(CollectionService:GetTagged("MapProp")) do
			if inst:IsA("Model") and inst:GetAttribute("MapPropId") == propId and not inst:IsDescendantOf(folder) and inst.Parent then
				local copy = inst:Clone()
				copy.Parent = inst.Parent
				local ref = Instance.new("ObjectValue")
				ref.Name = "_HoldParent"
				ref.Value = inst.Parent
				ref.Parent = inst
				inst.Parent = propHold
				held += 1
			end
		end
	end
	table.insert(lines, `  originals held: {held}`)
	install(propId, model)
	table.insert(lines, Sync.run({ only = { propId } }))
	return table.concat(lines, "\n")
end

-- puts back the held originals (each replaces the preview instance standing at its place) and the template that was
-- there before the preview (MapProps._Previous.<propId>), syncs, deletes the preview template and checks that no
-- preview MeshPart is left anywhere
function ApplyPropMeshes.endPreview(propId: string): string
	local Sync = fresh(devTool("SyncMapProps"))
	local folder = templateFolder()
	local current = folder:FindFirstChild(propId)
	local previous = folder:FindFirstChild("_Previous")
	local old = previous and previous:FindFirstChild(propId)
	local lines = { `ApplyPropMeshes.endPreview({propId})` }
	local hold = folder:FindFirstChild(HOLD)
	local propHold = hold and hold:FindFirstChild(propId)
	if propHold then
		local restored, lost = 0, 0
		for _, original in ipairs(propHold:GetChildren()) do
			local ref = original:FindFirstChild("_HoldParent")
			local parent = ref and (ref :: ObjectValue).Value
			if parent and original:IsA("Model") then
				local at = original:GetPivot().Position
				for _, c in ipairs(parent:GetChildren()) do
					if c:IsA("Model") and c.Name == original.Name and c:GetAttribute("MapPropId") == propId and (c:GetPivot().Position - at).Magnitude < 1e-3 then
						c:Destroy() -- the preview instance
						break
					end
				end
				(ref :: Instance):Destroy()
				original.Parent = parent
				restored += 1
			else
				lost += 1
			end
		end
		propHold:Destroy()
		if hold and #hold:GetChildren() == 0 then
			hold:Destroy()
		end
		table.insert(lines, `  originals put back: {restored}` .. (if lost > 0 then `, {lost} without a parent (left in MapProps)` else ""))
	end
	if old and old:GetAttribute(PREVIEW_ATTRIBUTE) then
		-- never put a preview back as the template (EditableMesh parts cannot be saved)
		old:Destroy()
		old = nil
		table.insert(lines, "  MapProps._Previous." .. propId .. " was itself a preview: removed, not restored")
	end
	if current and current:GetAttribute(PREVIEW_ATTRIBUTE) then
		current:Destroy()
		if old then
			old.Parent = folder
			table.insert(lines, "  previous template restored")
		elseif propHold then
			table.insert(lines, "  preview template removed (no template before the preview)")
		else
			table.insert(lines, "  no previous template: MapProps." .. propId .. " removed (the instances keep the preview until a template exists!)")
		end
	else
		table.insert(lines, "  the current template is not a preview: left as it is")
	end
	if previous and #previous:GetChildren() == 0 then
		previous:Destroy()
	end
	table.insert(lines, Sync.run({ only = { propId } }))
	-- preview MeshParts have no MeshId (EditableMesh content): none may stay in the place
	local left = 0
	for _, root in ipairs({ workspace, ServerStorage, ReplicatedStorage }) do
		for _, d in ipairs(root:GetDescendants()) do
			if d:IsA("MeshPart") and d.MeshId == "" then
				local ok, content = pcall(function()
					return (d :: any).MeshContent
				end)
				if ok and content and content.SourceType == Enum.ContentSourceType.Object then
					left += 1
					table.insert(lines, "  EDITABLE-MESH PART LEFT: " .. d:GetFullName())
				end
			end
		end
	end
	table.insert(lines, `  EditableMesh-backed MeshParts left in the place: {left}`)
	return table.concat(lines, "\n")
end

return ApplyPropMeshes
